{
 "duration": 24.707,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Two miles into her first overnight, Rosa's shoulders were burning.",
   "start": 0.4,
   "end": 3.967
  },
  {
   "text": "The hip belt hung loose around her waist, so the straps carried everything.",
   "start": 4.417,
   "end": 8.338
  },
  {
   "text": "Her friend fixed it in thirty seconds.",
   "start": 8.788,
   "end": 10.612
  },
  {
   "text": "Hip belt first, sitting on the hip bones, pulled snug.",
   "start": 11.062,
   "end": 14.058
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the shoulder straps, just firm.",
   "start": 14.508,
   "end": 16.266
  },
  {
   "text": "Heavy things packed close to your back.",
   "start": 16.716,
   "end": 18.345
  },
  {
   "text": "The weight dropped onto her hips, and her shoulders let go.",
   "start": 18.795,
   "end": 21.741
  },
  {
   "text": "Save this before your first night on the trail.",
   "start": 22.191,
   "end": 24.507
  }
 ],
